The generated `.mpy` regenerates byte-identically from `solution.py`. The differential found a real trusted-reference discrepancy: on any string ending in exactly two spaces, the candidate returns two underscores (matching the prompt’s prose), while `canonical.py` returns only one. There were 285 such mismatches in 10,366 cases; the candidate had zero mismatches against an independent direct contract oracle. I’ll carry this conflict into the adequacy judgment rather than hiding it.
